From: DANOS <noreply@danos.io>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 08:00:00 +0800
Subject: docs: fix two latent XSLT bugs exposed by the current xsltproc/libxslt

Both were masked until the libtirpc fix (danos/xdr-fallback-when-
libtirpc-pkgconfig-missing.patch) let the build reach doc generation
for the first time on this toolchain; verified locally afterward
against all 73 docs/*.html.in pages, 0 failures.

1) docs/site.xsl referenced $pagesrc and $timestamp at global scope
   (in the $href_base variable, and in <xsl:with-param select="$pagesrc"/>)
   without ever declaring them as top-level xsl:param -- they were only
   ever declared as local params on page.xsl's "page"-mode template.
   xsltproc's --stringparam pagesrc/--stringparam timestamp (see
   docs/meson.build) has nothing to bind to without a matching top-level
   xsl:param, leaving the global references undefined.

2) docs/page.xsl's text(), comment()|processing-instruction() and node()
   templates in mode="copy" are all "kind test" patterns, which XSLT
   gives the same default priority (-0.5). Which one wins a tie on a
   text/comment/PI node is then processor-defined, not spec-guaranteed.
   This build's xsltproc resolved the tie by dispatching text nodes into
   node()'s xsl:element branch instead, where name() of a text node is
   empty: "xsl:element: The effective name '' is not a valid QName."
   Giving the two more specific templates an explicit priority="1"
   removes the ambiguity outright, on any processor.
---
--- a/docs/site.xsl
+++ b/docs/site.xsl
@@ -13,6 +13,14 @@
     encoding="UTF-8"
     indent="yes"/>

+  <!-- Bound by xsltproc's stringparam options pagesrc and timestamp (see
+       docs/meson.build). Referenced below at global scope (in $href_base) and
+       passed on to page.xsl's "page"-mode template, so they must be declared
+       as top-level params here too, not only as that template's own local
+       params. -->
+  <xsl:param name="pagesrc"/>
+  <xsl:param name="timestamp"/>
+
   <xsl:variable name="href_base">
     <xsl:choose>
       <xsl:when test="$pagesrc = 'docs/404.html.in'">
--- a/docs/page.xsl
+++ b/docs/page.xsl
@@ -209,10 +209,22 @@
     </xsl:element>
   </xsl:template>

-  <xsl:template match="text()" mode="copy">
+  <!-- text(), comment()|processing-instruction() and node() below are all
+       "kind test" patterns, which XSLT gives the same default priority
+       (-0.5); which one wins a tie on a text/comment/PI node is then
+       processor-defined, not spec-guaranteed. Give the more specific ones an
+       explicit higher priority so a text node can no longer be dispatched to
+       node()'s xsl:element branch, where name() of a text node is empty and
+       xsltproc (unlike whatever this was last verified against) errors on
+       it: "xsl:element: The effective name '' is not a valid QName." -->
+  <xsl:template match="text()" mode="copy" priority="1">
     <xsl:value-of select="."/>
   </xsl:template>

+  <xsl:template match="comment()|processing-instruction()" mode="copy" priority="1">
+    <xsl:copy/>
+  </xsl:template>
+
   <xsl:template match="node()" mode="copy">
     <xsl:element name="{name()}">
       <xsl:copy-of select="./@*"/>
